            "title": "Is Active",
            "description": "False refuses password login without deleting the account."
          }
        },
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "type": "object",
        "title": "AccountUpdateIn",
        "description": "Fields an administrator may change. Every one optional; absent means unchanged.\n\n**`guardian_external_id` is deliberately absent**, and its absence is the whole design.\n`AccountIn` already refuses it on creation so that an extra column in an import sheet\ncannot silently become a records grant; an update route that accepted it would reopen\nexactly that door from the other side. Binding keeps its own route and its own audit\nevent because \"who decided this parent is that guardian\" has to stay a question with\none answer.\n\n`model_config = {\"extra\": \"forbid\"}` so a caller who sends `guardian_external_id`\nanyway is told no, rather than having it quietly dropped and believing it worked."
      },
      "ErrorOut": {
        "properties": {
          "code": {
            "type": "string",
            "title": "Code",
            "description": "not_authorized | locked | not_found | conflict | not_configured"
          },
          "message": {
            "type": "string",
            "title": "Message",
            "default": ""
          }
        },
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "code"
        ],
        "title": "ErrorOut",
        "description": "The body behind every refusal this service makes.\n\nOne envelope for all of them, whichever layer raised. A client parses one shape and\nbranches on `code`, never on how the error happened to be produced — see\n`identity/api/errors.py`, which is the only place a domain error becomes a status."
      },
      "GuardianBindingIn": {
        "properties": {
          "guardian_external_id": {
            "type": "string",
            "title": "Guardian External Id"
          }
        },
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "guardian_external_id"
        ],
        "title": "GuardianBindingIn",
        "description": "Binds a login to a guardian in the records facade.\n\nThe most sensitive write in the system. There is no self-service path to it: an\naccount that could name its own guardian id could read any family's records."
      },
